zΔ⚡b|-4|+{{lowercase%7Ctitle%3Ddiff}}|=1|-a|=1|-f|=1|-b|=1|-8|+n|=1|-f|+[[computing]],|=1|-f|+'''diff'''|=1|-f|+is|=1|-f|+a|=1|-f|+utility|=1|-f|+that|=1|-f|+outputs|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+differences|=1|-f|+between|=1|-f|+two|=1|-f|+text|=1|-f|+files.|=1|-d|=1|-1|+he|=1|-f|+program's|=1|-f|+output|=1|-f|+is|=1|-f|+also|=1|-f|+called|=1|-f|+a|=1|-f|+''diff''.|=1|-a|=1|-f|=1|-8|+%3D%3D|=1|-6|+sage%3D%3D|=1|-b|=1|-8|+t|=1|-f|+is|=1|-f|+invoked|=1|-f|+from|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+command|=1|-f|+line|=1|-f|+with|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+names|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+two|=1|-a|+files:|=1|-4|=1|-f|+diff|=1|-f|+firstone.txt|=1|-a|+secondone.txt|=1|-f|=1|-e|+%3D%3D%3D|=1|-5|+ormal|=1|-a|+output%3D%3D%3D|=1|-2|=1|-1|+he|=1|-f|+result|=1|-f|+might|=1|-f|+look|=1|-f|+like|=1|-a|+this:|=1|-4|=1|-a|+0a1,3|=1|-4|=1|-f|+>|=1|-d|=1|-1|+his|=1|-f|+is|=1|-f|+an|=1|-f|+important|=1|-f|+notice!|=1|-6|=1|-8|+t|=1|-a|+should|=1|-4|=1|-f|+>|=1|-f|+therefore|=1|-f|+be|=1|-f|+located|=1|-f|+at|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+beginning|=1|-a|+of|=1|-4|=1|-f|+>|=1|-f|+this|=1|-a|+document!|=1|-4|=1|-a|+7,12d9|=1|-4|=1|-f|+<|=1|-d|=1|-1|+his|=1|-f|+paragraph|=1|-f|+contains|=1|-f|+text|=1|-f|+that|=1|-a|+is|=1|-4|=1|-a|+< outdated %2D it will be deprecated and|=1|-4|+ < deleted in the near|=1|-a|+future.|=1|-2|+ < |=1|-1|+his is an important notice!|=1|-6|=1|-3|+t should|=1|-4|=1|-a|+< therefore be located at the beginning of|=1|-4|=1|-a|+< this document!|=1|-4|=1|-a|+14,15c11,14|=1|-1|+ < spell check this dokument. |=1|-2|+n|=1|-a|+the other|=1|-4|+ < hand,|=1|-6|=1|-3|+ could do with some shoarma.|=1|-4|=1|-a|+%2D%2D%2D|=1|-1|+ > spell check this document. |=1|-2|+n the|=1|-a|+other|=1|-4|+ > hand,|=1|-6|=1|-3|+ could do with some shoarma.|=1|-2|+ > |=1|-1|+his paragraph contains important|=1|-a|+new|=1|-4|=1|-6|+> additions to this document.%0A%0A|=1|-8|+n this ''normal diff output'',|=1|-f|+'''a'''|=1|-f|+stands|=1|-f|+for|=1|-f|+''added'',|=1|-f|+'''d'''|=1|-f|+for|=1|-f|+''deleted''|=1|-f|+and|=1|-f|+'''c'''|=1|-f|+for|=1|-f|+''changed''.|=1|-4|=1|-a|+y|=1|-f|+default,|=1|-f|+lines|=1|-f|+common|=1|-f|+to|=1|-f|+both|=1|-f|+files|=1|-f|+are|=1|-f|+not|=1|-f|+shown.|=1|-5|=1|-9|+ines|=1|-f|+that|=1|-f|+have|=1|-f|+moved|=1|-f|+will|=1|-f|+show|=1|-f|+up|=1|-f|+as|=1|-f|+added|=1|-f|+on|=1|-f|+their|=1|-f|+new|=1|-f|+location|=1|-f|+and|=1|-f|+as|=1|-f|+deleted|=1|-f|+on|=1|-f|+their|=1|-f|+old|=1|-a|+location.|=1|-f|=1|-8|+%3D%3D%3D|=1|-b|+nified|=1|-a|+format%3D%3D%3D|=1|-b|=1|-8|+n|=1|-f|+''unified|=1|-f|+format''|=1|-f|+(or|=1|-a|+''unidiff''), each line that occurs only in the first file is preceded by a minus sign, each line that occurs only in the second file is preceded by a plus sign, and common lines are preceded by a space.|=1|-2|+%0ALines beginning with three plus signs indicate the number of lines in each ''hunk'', the file names, and where in the files to find them.  |=1|-1|+his|=1|-3|+output is often used as input to the [[patch (|=1|+nix)%7Cpatch]] program.%0A%0A%3D%3D%3D|=1|-5|+inary file support%3D%3D%3D|=1|-2|=1|-1|+he first editions of the diff program were designed for line comparisons of text|=1|-4|+files expecting the [[newline]] character to delimit lines.  |=1|-5|+y the 1980s, necessary support for binary files resulted in a shift in the application's design and implementation.|=1|-2|+%0A%3D%3DHistory%3D%3D%0A|=1|-1|+he|=1|-3|+'''diff''' program was developed in the early 1970s on the [[|=1|-4|+nix]] operating system which was emerging from [[|=1|-4|+T&|=1|-1|+]]|=1|-4|+[[|=1|+ell |=1|-3|+abs]] in Murray Hill, |=1|-3|+ew Jersey.  |=1|-1|+he final version,|=1|-1|+first shipped with the 5th |=1|-1|+dition of |=1|-2|+nix in 1974, was entirely written by [[Douglas Mc|=1|-6|+lroy]].  |=1|-1|+his|=1|-6|+research was published in a 1976 paper co%2Dwritten with [[James W. Hunt]] who developed an initial prototype of diff.%0A%0AMc|=1|+lroy's work was preceded and influenced by [[Stephen |=1|-7|+. Johnson%7CSteve Johnson]]'s comparison program on|=1|-1|+[[G|=1|-5|=1|-4|=1|-2|+S]] and [[Mike|=1|-5|=1|-9|+esk]]'s '''proof'''|=1|-2|+program.  '''|=1|+roof''' originated on |=1|-9|+nix and produced line%2Dby%2Dline changes like diff and even used angle%2Dbrackets (">" and "<") for presenting line insertions and deletions in the program's output.  |=1|-1|+he [[heuristic]]s used|=1|-d|+in these early applications were deemed unreliable though.  |=1|-1|+he potential usefulness of a diff tool provoked|=1|-6|+Mc|=1|-8|+lroy into researching|=1|-2|+and designing a more robust tool that could be used in a variety of tasks but perform well in the processing and space limitations of the [[|=1|-1|+DP%2D11]]'s hardware.  His approach resulted from collaboration also with individuals at |=1|+ell |=1|-2|+abs including [[|=1|-6|+lfred|=1|-8|=1|-6|+ho]],|=1|-1|+[[|=1|+lliot |=1|+inson]], [[Jeffrey |=1|-2|+llman]], and [[Harold S. Stone]].%0A%0A|=1|-8|+n the context of|=1|-3|=1|-9|+nix, the use of the [[ed]] line editor provided diff with the natural ability to create machine%2Dusable "edit scripts".  |=1|-1|+hese edit scripts, when saved to a file, can, along with the original file, be reconstituted by '''ed''' into the modified file in its entirety. |=1|-d|=1|-1|+his greatly reduced the space necessary to maintain multiple versions|=1|-6|+of a file.  Mc|=1|-3|+lroy considered writing a post%2Dprocessor for diff where a variety of output formats could be designed and implemented, but he found it more frugal and simpler to have diff be responsible for generating the syntax and reverse%2Dorder input accepted by the '''ed''' command.|=1|-4|+In|=1|-5|+1985, [[|=1|-9|+arry Wall]] composed a separate utility, [[patch|=1|-3|+(|=1|-2|+nix) %7C patch]], that generalized and extended the ability to modify files with diff output.%0A%0A|=1|-8|+n diff's early years, common uses included comparing changes in programming language source code, source to technical documents, verifying program debugging output, comparing filesystem listings and analyzing computer assembly|=1|-f|+code.|=1|-f|=1|-d|=1|-1|+he|=1|-f|+output|=1|-f|+targeted|=1|-f|+for|=1|-f|+'''ed'''|=1|-f|+was|=1|-f|+motivated|=1|-f|+to|=1|-f|+provide|=1|-f|+compression|=1|-f|+for|=1|-f|+a|=1|-f|+sequence|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+modifications|=1|-f|+made|=1|-f|+to|=1|-f|+a|=1|-f|+file.|=1|-f|=1|-d|=1|-1|+he|=1|-7|+[[S|=1|-f|=1|-7|+S%7CSource|=1|-7|=1|-7|+ode|=1|-7|=1|-7|+ontrol|=1|-f|+System]]|=1|-7|+(S|=1|-f|=1|-7|+S)|=1|-f|+emerged|=1|-f|+in|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+late|=1|-f|+1970s|=1|-f|+as|=1|-f|+a|=1|-f|+direct|=1|-f|+consequence|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+this|=1|-a|+development.|=1|-f|=1|-d|=1|-6|=1|-f|+conceptual|=1|-f|+predecessor|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+diff|=1|-f|+includes|=1|-2|+[[|=1|-c|+roject|=1|-f|+Xanadu]],|=1|-f|+a|=1|-f|+hypertext|=1|-f|+project|=1|-f|+established|=1|-f|+in|=1|-f|+1960|=1|-f|+that|=1|-f|+had|=1|-f|+envisioned|=1|-f|+a|=1|-f|+version|=1|-f|+tracking|=1|-f|+system|=1|-f|+necessary|=1|-f|+for|=1|-f|+its|=1|-f|+"transpointing|=1|-f|+windows"|=1|-f|+feature.|=1|-f|=1|-8|=1|-6|+s|=1|-f|+part|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+this|=1|-f|+feature,|=1|-f|+file|=1|-f|+differences|=1|-f|+were|=1|-f|+subsumed|=1|-f|+in|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+expansive|=1|-f|+term|=1|-f|+"[[transclusion]]",|=1|-f|+when|=1|-f|+a|=1|-f|+document|=1|-f|+has|=1|-f|+included|=1|-f|+in|=1|-f|+it|=1|-f|+parts|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+other|=1|-f|+documents|=1|-f|+or|=1|-a|+revisions.|=1|-f|=1|-b|=1|-8|+n|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+digital|=1|-f|+realm|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+humanities,|=1|-f|+computer|=1|-f|+comparison|=1|-f|+systems|=1|-f|+were|=1|-f|+understood|=1|-f|+to|=1|-f|+have|=1|-f|+been|=1|-f|+created|=1|-f|+for|=1|-f|+working|=1|-f|+on|=1|-f|+literary|=1|-f|+works|=1|-f|+published|=1|-f|+as|=1|-f|+large|=1|-a|+volumes.|=1|-f|=1|+%3D%3D%3D|=1|-e|+ariations%3D%3D%3D|=1|-4|+Most|=1|-f|+diff|=1|-f|+implementations|=1|-f|+remain|=1|-f|+outwardly|=1|-f|+unchanged|=1|-f|+since|=1|-f|+1975.|=1|-f|=1|-d|=1|-1|+he|=1|-f|+modifications|=1|-f|+include|=1|-f|+improvements|=1|-f|+to|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+core|=1|-f|+algorithm,|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+addition|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+useful|=1|-f|+features|=1|-f|+to|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+command,|=1|-f|+and|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+design|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+new|=1|-f|+output|=1|-f|+formats.|=1|-d|=1|-1|+he|=1|-f|+basic|=1|-f|+algorithm|=1|-f|+is|=1|-f|+described|=1|-f|+in|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+papers|=1|-8|+''|=1|-6|+n|=1|-c|=1|-c|+(|=1|-5|+D)|=1|-f|+Difference|=1|-8|=1|-6|+lgorithm|=1|-f|+and|=1|-f|+its|=1|-b|=1|-3|+ariations''|=1|-f|+by|=1|-1|=1|-d|+ugene|=1|-f|+W.|=1|-f|+Myers|=1|-f|+and|=1|-f|+in|=1|-8|+''|=1|-6|=1|-f|+File|=1|-7|=1|-7|+omparison|=1|-2|=1|-c|+rogram''|=1|-f|+by|=1|-f|+Webb|=1|-f|+Miller|=1|-f|+and|=1|-f|+Myers.|=1|-f|=1|-d|=1|-1|+he|=1|-f|+algorithm|=1|-f|+was|=1|-f|+independently|=1|-f|+discovered|=1|-f|+as|=1|-f|+described|=1|-f|+in|=1|-8|+''|=1|-6|+lgorithms|=1|-f|+for|=1|-8|=1|-6|+pproximate|=1|-f|+String|=1|-f|+Matching'',|=1|-1|+[[|=1|-d|+.|=1|-3|=1|-6|+kkonen]].|=1|-f|=1|-7|=1|-c|+ostprocessors|=1|-f|+'''sdiff'''|=1|-f|+and|=1|-f|+'''diffmk'''|=1|-f|+render|=1|-f|+side%2Dby%2Dside|=1|-f|+diff|=1|-f|+listings|=1|-f|+and|=1|-f|+applied|=1|-f|+change|=1|-f|+marks|=1|-f|+to|=1|-f|+printed|=1|-f|+documents,|=1|-f|+respectively.|=1|-f|=1|-4|=1|-a|+oth|=1|-f|+were|=1|-f|+developed|=1|-f|+elsewhere|=1|-f|+in|=1|-4|=1|-a|+ell|=1|-5|=1|-9|+abs|=1|-f|+in|=1|-f|+or|=1|-f|+before|=1|-a|+1981.|=1|-f|=1|-2|=1|-1|+he|=1|-4|+[[|=1|-f|+SD%7C|=1|-a|+erkeley|=1|-f|+distribution|=1|-f|+of|=1|-3|=1|-b|+nix]]|=1|-f|+made|=1|-f|+a|=1|-f|+point|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+adding|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+context|=1|-f|+format|=1|-7|+(%2D|=1|-7|+)|=1|-f|+and|=1|-f|+the|=1|-f|+ability|=1|-f|+to|=1|-f|+recurse|=1|-f|+on|=1|-f|+filesystem|=1|-f|+directory|=1|-f|+structures|=1|-f|+(%2Dr),|=1|-f|+adding|=1|-f|+those|=1|-f|+features|=1|-f|+in|=1|-f|+2.8|=1|-4|=1|-a|+SD,|=1|-f|+released|=1|-f|+in|=1|-f|+July|=1|-a|+1981.|=1|-f|=1|-2|=1|-1|+he|=1|-f|+context|=1|-f|+format|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+diff|=1|-f|+introduced|=1|-f|+at|=1|-4|=1|-a|+erkeley|=1|-f|+helped|=1|-f|+with|=1|-f|+distributing|=1|-f|+patches|=1|-f|+for|=1|-f|+source|=1|-f|+code|=1|-f|+that|=1|-f|+may|=1|-f|+have|=1|-f|+been|=1|-f|+changed|=1|-a|+minimally.|=1|-f|=1|-7|+[[|=1|-c|+aul|=1|-f|+Jensen]],|=1|-f|+faced|=1|-f|+with|=1|-f|+consolidating|=1|-f|+changes|=1|-f|+from|=1|-f|+two|=1|-f|+branches|=1|-f|+of|=1|-f|+a|=1|-f|+program's|=1|-f|+source|=1|-f|+code|=1|-f|+tree|=1|-f|+proposed|=1|-f|+[[diff3]],|=1|-f|+which|=1|-f|+persists|=1|-f|+for|=1|-225a|+most as a curiosity, but is still useful to those finding themselves in Jensen's situation.%0A%0AUnified context diffs were originally developed by [[Wayne Davison]] in August 1990 (in '''unidiff''' which appeared in Volume 14 of comp.sources.misc).  [[Richard Stallman]] added unified diff support to [[GNU%7CGNU Project]]'s diff utility one month later, and the feature debuted in '''GNU diff''' 1.15, released in January 1991. GNU diff has since generalized the context format to allow arbitrary formatting of diffs.  GNU diff is included in the diffutils package with other diff and [[Patch (Unix)%7Cpatch]] related utilities.%0A%0A%3D%3D%3DRelated proprietary software%3D%3D%3D%0A[[MS%2DDOS]] 3.30 and later and all versions of [[Microsoft Windows]] have an '''fc''' (File Compare) command. Whenever '''fc''' encounters a difference between the two files it is presented in the following format:%0A ***** old.txt%0A deleted lines%0A ***** NEW.TXT%0A inserted lines%0A *****%0ANote that '''fc''' capitalizes the filename of the second file. This format is not useful as input for other computer programs.  Line notations are missing, but more problematic for an algorithm is the output of filenames by '''fc''' which is indistinguishable from an inserted or deleted line beginning with five asterisks and a space. Such a line may occur in a file that was produced by or discusses '''fc''' itself.%0A%0A[[Mac OS X]] includes the graphical '''FileMerge''' program from Apple in the developer tools package.  This program offers automatic file merging, but is most useful as a simple but powerful manual merge tool for text based files.  '''FileMerge''' expects Unix style [[newline]]s.%0A%0A%3D%3DFree software implementations%3D%3D%0AThe [[GNU]] Project has an implementation of diff (and diff3) that is available from the [http://www.gnu.org/software/diffutils/diffutils.html GNU diffutils] package.%0A%0ASeveral tools on various platforms use the GNU diffutils engine and provide a graphical display, and some combine editing and merging capabilities. The following are some of these [[free software%7Cfree]] tools.%0A%0A*[[Emacs]] %2D Provided by [[Ediff]] mode.%0A*[[VimDiff]] [http://vim.sourceforge.net/htmldoc/diff.html]%0A*[[gtkdiff]] [http://home.catv.ne.jp/pp/ginoue/software/gtkdiff/index%2De.html]%0A*''KDiff3'' [http://kdiff3.sourceforge.net]%0A*[[kompare]]%0A*[[Meld]]%0A*[[tkdiff]] [http://tkdiff.sourceforge.net]%0A*[[WinMerge]]%0A*[[xxdiff]] [http://xxdiff.sourceforge.net]%0A%0A%3D%3DProprietary Implementations%3D%3D%0AOther [[proprietary software%7Cproprietary]] file comparison utilities include:%0A%0A*For [[Microsoft Windows]]%0A**[[Altova DiffDog]] [http://www.altova.com/products_diffdog.html]%0A**[[Araxis merge]] [http://www.araxis.com/]%0A**[[BeyondCompare]] [http://scootersoftware.com]%0A**[[Compare It!]] [http://www.grigsoft.com/]%0A**[[ExamDiff Pro]] [http://www.prestosoft.com/ps.asp?page%3Dedp_examdiffpro]%0A**[[ExamDiff]] [http://www.prestosoft.com/ps.asp?page%3Dedp_examdiff]%0A**[[P4WinMerge]] [http://www.perforce.com/perforce/products/p4winmerge.html] %2D a component of the [http://www.perforce.com/ Perforce SCM System].%0A**[[Stylus Studio]] [http://www.stylusstudio.com/xml_differencing.html]%0A**[[WinDiff]]%0A*For Macintosh:%0A**[[Differences Examiner]] [http://alphaomega.software.free.fr/]%0A**[[Apple FileMerge]] (part of free Apple Developer Tools)%0A%0A%3D%3DSee also%3D%3D%0A*[[Cmp%7C"cmp" command]]%0A*[[Delta encoding]]%0A*[[Levenshtein distance]]%0A*[[Longest%2Dcommon subsequence problem]]%0A*[[Patch (Unix)%7CPatch]]%0A*[[Revision Control System]]%0A*[[Software configuration management%7CSoftware configuration management (SCM)]]%0A*[[Source Code Control System]]%0A%0A%3D%3DReferences%3D%3D%0A*{{journal reference%7CAuthor%3DHunt, James W. and McIlroy, M. Douglas%7CTitle%3D[http://www.cs.dartmouth.edu/~doug/ An Algorithm for Differential File Comparison]%7CVolume%3D41%7CJournal%3DComputing Science Technical Report, Bell Laboratories%7CYear%3DJune 1976%7CPages%3D}} %0A*{{book reference%7CTitle%3D[http://www.gnu.org/software/diffutils/manual/ Comparing and Merging Files with GNU Diff and Patch]%7CAuthor%3DDavid MacKenzie, Paul Eggert, and Richard Stallman%7CID%3DISBN 0954161750%7CPublisher%3D%7CYear%3D1997}} %0A*{{journal reference issue%7CAuthor%3DE. Myers%7CTitle%3D[http://citeseer.ist.psu.edu/myers86ond.html An O(ND) Difference Algorithm and Its Variations]%7CJournal%3DAlgorithmica%7CVolume%3D1%7CIssue%3D2%7CYear%3D1986%7CPages%3D251%2D266}} %0A*{{journal reference issue%7CAuthor%3DWebb Miller and Eugene W. Myers%7CTitle%3DA File Comparison Program%7CJournal%3DSoftware%2D%2DPractice and Experience%7CVolume%3D15%7CIssue%3D11%7CYear%3D1985%7CPages%3D1025%2D1040}}%0A*{{journal reference%7CAuthor%3DE. Ukkonen%7CTitle%3DAlgorithms for Approximate String Matching%7CVolume%3D64%7CJournal%3DInformation and Control%7CYear%3D1985%7CPages%3D100%2D118}}%0A*A generic implementation of the Myers SES/LCS algorithm with the Hirschberg linear space refinement [http://www.ioplex.com/~miallen/libmba/dl/src/diff.c (C source code)]%0A%0A%3D%3DExternal links%3D%3D%0A*[http://www.gnu.org/software/diffutils/diffutils.html GNU Diff utilities]. Made available by the [[Free Software Foundation]]. Free Documentation. Free source code.%0A*{{dmoz%7CComputers/Software/File_Management/File_Comparison/%7CFile Comparison}}%0A*[http://unixhelp.ed.ac.uk/CGI/man%2Dcgi?diff diff(1)] %2D The program's [[manpage]]%0A%0A[[Category:Unix software]]%0A[[Category:File comparison tools]]%0A%0A[[ang:Diff]]%0A[[de:Diff]]%0A[[fr:Diff]]|
