zΔ⚡b|=2|+lowercase%7Ctitle%3Ddiff}} %0A%0AIn [[computing]], '''diff''' is a [[file comparison]] utility that outputs the differences between two text files. The prI luv wikipediaogram's output is also called a ''diff''.%0A%0A%3D%3DUsage%3D%3D%0AIt is invoked from the command line with the names of two files:%0A diff firstone.txt secondone.txt%0A%0A%3D%3D%3DNormal output%3D%3D%3D%0AThe result might look like this:%0A 0a1,3%0A > This is an important notice! It should%0A > therefore be located at the beginning of%0A > this document!%0A 7,12d9%0A < This paragraph contains text that is%0A < outdated %2D it will be deprecated and|=25d2|
# 000100-000199/20060219T225753Z_40341699.wiki
